From: GT-BE98 mainline OS <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] DEBUG: ubi: write fence (ubi.fence=<volumes>)

GT-BE98 mainline development OS, not for upstream (NAND-PHASE2.md).

With ubi.fence=<name>[,...] (runtime parameter, for devices attached
afterwards) UBI only writes or erases PEBs that are free or belong to a fenced
volume. PEBs of other volumes and attach erase-candidates not owned by a
fenced volume go to a fence_off tree: never moved by wear-leveling, never
scrubbed (scrub requests are refused, the data stays readable), never erased.
Only fenced volumes accept LEB writes, unmaps and atomic changes, so the
volume table cannot change. Bad-block marking is refused; fastmap must be
disabled; every write is refused until the fence is set up. UBI I/O registers
each program/erase as in flight for the MTD write fence (the NAND core gate).
Every allowed write/erase is logged (rate-limited) with PEB and owner;
debugfs ubi/ubiN/fence has the state and counters. debugfs ubi/fence_restore
lets a root process rewrite listed PEBs of a chip no UBI device is attached
to (raw backup restore).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/mtd/ubi/Makefile b/drivers/mtd/ubi/Makefile
index 4b51aaf00..ec815597b 100644
--- a/drivers/mtd/ubi/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/mtd/ubi/Makefile
@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@
 obj-$(CONFIG_MTD_UBI) += ubi.o
 
 ubi-y += vtbl.o vmt.o upd.o build.o cdev.o kapi.o eba.o io.o wl.o attach.o
-ubi-y += misc.o debug.o
+ubi-y += misc.o debug.o fence.o
 ubi-$(CONFIG_MTD_UBI_FASTMAP) += fastmap.o
 ubi-$(CONFIG_MTD_UBI_BLOCK) += block.o
 
diff --git a/drivers/mtd/ubi/build.c b/drivers/mtd/ubi/build.c
index 456090a12..bb46c3b0a 100644
--- a/drivers/mtd/ubi/build.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/ubi/build.c
@@ -1001,6 +1001,10 @@ int ubi_attach_mtd_dev(struct mtd_info *mtd, int ubi_num,
 	if (!ubi->fm_buf)
 		goto out_free;
 #endif
+	err = ubi_fence_attach_begin(ubi);
+	if (err)
+		goto out_free;
+
 	err = ubi_attach(ubi, disable_fm ? 1 : 0);
 	if (err) {
 		ubi_err(ubi, "failed to attach mtd%d, error %d",
@@ -1367,6 +1371,11 @@ static int __init ubi_init(void)
 	if (err)
 		goto out_slab;
 
+	/* GT-BE98: the UBI fence is the only writer of fenced NAND chips */
+	err = ubi_fence_register();
+	if (err)
+		pr_warn("UBI: cannot register the write fence, error %d\n", err);
+
 	err = ubiblock_init();
 	if (err) {
 		pr_err("UBI error: block: cannot initialize, error %d\n", err);
@@ -1416,6 +1425,7 @@ static void __exit ubi_exit(void)
 			ubi_detach_mtd_dev(ubi_devices[i]->ubi_num, 1);
 			mutex_unlock(&ubi_devices_mutex);
 		}
+	ubi_fence_unregister();
 	ubi_debugfs_exit();
 	kmem_cache_destroy(ubi_wl_entry_slab);
 	misc_deregister(&ubi_ctrl_cdev);
